.TH FL-LOGS 1 "November 2026" "fldesktop 0.1.4" "fldesktop"
.SH NAME
fl-logs \- log viewer
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfl-logs\fR [\fB\-\-user\fR | \fIFILE\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Shows the systemd journal (the system's, or yours with \fB\-\-user\fR) for
this boot, the boot before, the last hour, today or the last week, or a log
file in \fI/var/log\fR (syslog, messages, OpenRC's \fIrc.log\fR) on systems
without systemd. Entries are coloured by priority (errors red, warnings
yellow) and can be filtered by priority, program and text; new entries
appear as they come (Follow). Selecting an entry shows all its fields; the
shown entries can be saved as text.
.PP
Reading the system journal needs membership of the \fBsystemd-journal\fR or
\fBadm\fR group; reading the files in \fI/var/log\fR may need \fBadm\fR.
.SH CRASH REPORTS
When an fldesktop program crashes it writes a short report (program, version,
system, signal and a backtrace) to \fI$XDG_STATE_HOME/fldesktop/crashes\fR
(\fI~/.local/state/fldesktop/crashes\fR) before the system's core dump
handler runs. \fBCrashes…\fR lists them, with the core dumps of fl-* programs
that \fBcoredumpctl\fR(1) knows of; \fBReport on GitHub…\fR opens a new
issue in the web browser with the report filled in (look at it before sending;
nothing is sent by itself). Set \fBFLD_NO_CRASH_HANDLER=1\fR to turn the reports off.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBjournalctl\fR(1), \fBfl-services\fR(1)
